{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345172",
      "title": "React Projects Use a Build Process",
      "sourceHash": "a541ddfa832bbe18c6697148c498aa8b01c706706a98f1985c77767e7d9fb2dd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "Now, if you take a look at a React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "like this React demo I showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 9.69,
          "en": "in the first course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.69,
          "end": 13.26,
          "en": "to which you again, find a link attached to this lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.26,
          "end": 15.54,
          "en": "if you take a look at such a project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.54,
          "end": 20.54,
          "en": "you'll note that in the annex html file that you find there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.82,
          "end": 24.24,
          "en": "you won't find any script tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.24,
          "end": 28.8,
          "en": "There in this index html file in the head section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 32.43,
          "en": "I have some meta tags and I have link tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.43,
          "end": 35.04,
          "en": "but I have no script tag there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.04,
          "end": 38.01,
          "en": "And in the body, I just have the no script tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.01,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "that shows a fallback message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "if the user has disabled JavaScript in their browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 46.53,
          "en": "but I got no script tag in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 48.93,
          "en": "Absolutely no script text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.93,
          "end": 52.65,
          "en": "and we also never add script text to that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.65,
          "end": 54.78,
          "en": "Nonetheless, as you can of course tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.78,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "if I reload this here, this app works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 60.81,
          "en": "and JavaScript code clearly is executing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.81,
          "end": 63.57,
          "en": "because the React app is executing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.57,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "And React of course, in the end, is JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 70.56,
          "en": "A special JavaScript code, but it is JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.56,
          "end": 72.3,
          "en": "So why is this working?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.3,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "Well, because as mentioned at the end of the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 80.4,
          "en": "React projects use a build process, which simply means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.4,
          "end": 85.08,
          "en": "the code you write is not the code that gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.08,
          "end": 88.23,
          "en": "like this, at least, in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.23,
          "end": 92.97,
          "en": "Instead, the code you write is transformed behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.97,
          "end": 96,
          "en": "before it's handed off to the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96,
          "end": 99.24000000000001,
          "en": "In this demo project on CodeSandbox,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.24000000000001,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "but also in the local projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 103.53,
          "en": "I'll use throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.53,
          "end": 105.81,
          "en": "this is done with help of a tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.81,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "that's running in the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 109.97999999999999,
          "en": "And you can actually see that tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "in the package.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "This file simply lists all the dependencies of this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 118.77000000000001,
          "en": "all the libraries used by that project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.77000000000001,
          "end": 120.54,
          "en": "and therefore, of course, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.54,
          "end": 124.89,
          "en": "in there we find the React libraries, the two packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.89,
          "end": 128.07,
          "en": "that make up the React library to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "But here in this example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 134.4,
          "en": "we also find the React Scripts library in addition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.4,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "And this is actually a library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 139.38,
          "en": "that's not going to be executed in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.38,
          "end": 143.1,
          "en": "or that's used by React once it's running in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.1,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "but instead this React Scripts package here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "provides a bunch of tools that take your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 153.81,
          "en": "and transform it behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.81,
          "end": 156.75,
          "en": "before it's then injected into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.75,
          "end": 160.05,
          "en": "Or to be precise, before it's then injected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 164.13,
          "en": "with help of a script tag into the HTML file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.13,
          "end": 166.59,
          "en": "If you take a look at this running website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.59,
          "end": 169.29,
          "en": "for example, by opening it in a new window,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.29,
          "end": 172.89,
          "en": "and you then there inspect this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.89,
          "end": 175.5,
          "en": "so that the browser developer tools open up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.5,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "you'll see that now there are some script tags in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 182.52,
          "en": "Actually multiple script tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.52,
          "end": 186.66,
          "en": "And these script elements were generated and injected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.66,
          "end": 190.2,
          "en": "into this HTML file automatically behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.2,
          "end": 194.73,
          "en": "by this built process that's running in the background.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.73,
          "end": 198.03,
          "en": "This preview website, which we see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 198.03,
          "end": 200.52,
          "en": "is being served by a development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.52,
          "end": 204.24,
          "en": "that's also running in the background on CodeSandbox.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.24,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "In a local project on the upper hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 210.12,
          "en": "you had to explicitly start that development server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.12,
          "end": 211.92000000000002,
          "en": "And it's this development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.92000000000002,
          "end": 215.22,
          "en": "which is watching your source code behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.22,
          "end": 218.28,
          "en": "and which is then also kind of transforming that source code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 222.51,
          "en": "behind the scenes and which is then adjusting the HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.51,
          "end": 224.73,
          "en": "to contain these script elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.73,
          "end": 228.6,
          "en": "that do then load that transformed source code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.6,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "So that the transformed source code is executed on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 235.5,
          "en": "And why do we use such a built process?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.5,
          "end": 238.77,
          "en": "Why does the code need to be transformed?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.77,
          "end": 241.35,
          "en": "Well, for two main reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.35,
          "end": 246.09,
          "en": "The first reason is that raw unprocessed React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.09,
          "end": 248.73,
          "en": "won't execute in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.73,
          "end": 253.73,
          "en": "Mostly because React code uses this special JSX feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255,
          "end": 257.67,
          "en": "Now, you will learn more about writing React code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.67,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "and about JSX later once we start diving into React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 266.52,
          "en": "JSX code simply is this HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.52,
          "end": 268.95,
          "en": "written in JavaScript files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.95,
          "end": 271.41,
          "en": "Out of the box, this would not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.41,
          "end": 274.8,
          "en": "because this is not a standard JavaScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.8,
          "end": 277.8,
          "en": "If you would try to use this kind of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.8,
          "end": 280.95,
          "en": "in our default JavaScript project here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 280.95,
          "end": 282.99,
          "en": "for example in the AppJS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.99,
          "end": 287.07,
          "en": "if you would try to add like a a div in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.07,
          "end": 289.87,
          "en": "and you would open this website preview",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 290.97,
          "end": 293.22,
          "en": "and try to reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.22,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "you would see that you would get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 300.03,
          "en": "An error that in the end points at this div here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 303.3,
          "en": "Because this indeed is not a standard JavaScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 303.3,
          "end": 305.463,
          "en": "it does not work out of the box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 306.69,
          "end": 309.81,
          "en": "So for that reason, to enable this syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.81,
          "end": 313.59,
          "en": "which is crucial in React apps as you will learn,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 313.59,
          "end": 316.32,
          "en": "because React will be all about including",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.32,
          "end": 320.58,
          "en": "this HTML-like code in your JavaScript files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 320.58,
          "end": 323.91,
          "en": "to enable this feature, the code must be transformed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 323.91,
          "end": 326.79,
          "en": "so that you can use it whilst writing the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.79,
          "end": 330.09,
          "en": "but it's transformed to something JavaScript knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330.09,
          "end": 333.09000000000003,
          "en": "before the code gets executed in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.09000000000003,
          "end": 336.24,
          "en": "That's one reason for using a build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 336.24,
          "end": 339.03,
          "en": "Another reason is that the code you write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 339.03,
          "end": 341.4,
          "en": "would not be optimized for production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 341.4,
          "end": 344.55,
          "en": "it would not be minified, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 344.55,
          "end": 347.34000000000003,
          "en": "Minification simply means that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.34000000000003,
          "end": 351.51,
          "en": "names of variables or functions are shortened",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 351.51,
          "end": 354.33,
          "en": "to reduce the amount of JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 354.33,
          "end": 356.25,
          "en": "that's served to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 356.25,
          "end": 357.96,
          "en": "If you take a look at the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 357.96,
          "end": 360.24,
          "en": "that is served to the user here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 360.24,
          "end": 364.17,
          "en": "by, for example, visiting one of these imported code files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 364.17,
          "end": 366.69,
          "en": "that is served here in CodeSandbox,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 366.69,
          "end": 369.51,
          "en": "you'll see that it looks something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.51,
          "end": 370.8,
          "en": "Pretty unreadable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.8,
          "end": 372.96,
          "en": "not the kind of code we would like to work on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.96,
          "end": 377.04,
          "en": "as a developer, but valid JavaScript code in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 377.04,
          "end": 380.25,
          "en": "Though it is code that's highly optimized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 380.25,
          "end": 384.06,
          "en": "to be as short and small as possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384.06,
          "end": 385.95,
          "en": "to reduce the amount of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.95,
          "end": 389.31,
          "en": "that has to be downloaded by the website visitor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 389.31,
          "end": 391.86,
          "en": "So that's another reason why React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 391.86,
          "end": 394.68,
          "en": "typically require a built process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 394.68,
          "end": 397.89,
          "en": "And the good news are that if you create a React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 397.89,
          "end": 399.51,
          "en": "on CodeSandbox",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.51,
          "end": 404.07,
          "en": "or with help of tools like Create React app or Vite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 404.07,
          "end": 405.84000000000003,
          "en": "so if you're using projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 405.84000000000003,
          "end": 407.79,
          "en": "as we're using them in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.79,
          "end": 411.81,
          "en": "those projects all come with such a built process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 411.81,
          "end": 415.2,
          "en": "So you don't have to go through any custom setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 415.2,
          "end": 417.54,
          "en": "or tweak anything on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 417.54,
          "end": 420.15,
          "en": "But that's also the reason why you also need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 420.15,
          "end": 422.37,
